data: {"type":"tool-output-available","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-ab23e6baae71babc","output":{"output":"Found 21 matches in 1 file\n\n[github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-billing] README.md:\n  25: Process payments using multiple payment modes (cash, insurance, mobile money, credit/debit cards, custom modes) with support for partial payments, payment attributes, automatic change calculation, and per-payment cashier attribution.\n  33: Manage multiple cashier stations/locations with cash point assignment for cashiers and location-based transaction tracking.\n  37: Track cashier shifts with clock in/out functionality, configurable timesheet validation for bill creation, auto-close timesheets, and shift-based reporting.\n  102: └── cashieritemprices/cashierItemPrices.csv\n  147: The forms of payment a cashier can accept. `attributes` is optional and defines the extra fields captured with a\n  159: The cashier stations bills are raised at. `location` references an existing location, so define your locations in the\n  190: Test and drug orders are billed automatically — nobody has to raise the bill in the cashier app. Saving an order\n  219: In `cashieritemprices/cashierItemPrices.csv`:\n  243: In `cashieritemprices/cashierItemPrices.csv`:\n  328:   order is priced. You keep their cashier and cash point resolution. The exemption check sits inside the method you\n  360: manage, purge), timesheet management (view, manage, purge), and app access for OpenMRS 2.x (cashier app, tasks,\n  373: | `billing.defaultShiftReportId`         | —                                                                 | ID of the Jasper cashier shift report                                                                                             |\n  186: [cashieritemprices](https://github.com/mekomsolutions/openmrs-module-initializer/blob/main/readme/cashieritemprices.md).\n  232: Drug orders can be priced through the **stock item** linked to the ordered drug in the Stock Management module or from your `cashieritemprices` configuration.\n  236: 1. a `cashieritemprices` row whose `Stock Item` is that stock item — the price you configured, if not,\n  240: So pricing drugs in `cashieritemprices` is optional. Leave the rows out and patients are billed the purchase price","sources":[{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-billing","path":"README.md","name":"README.md","revision":"HEAD"}]}}

